# Netlify reads this file from the publish directory, which is site/ (set by
# the root netlify.toml; see ADR-0007). Redirect rules in a netlify.toml would
# take precedence over it, but ours defines none.
#
# The site answers on two hostnames: the custom domain and the Netlify
# subdomain it was first deployed to. Both served 200, so the whole site
# existed twice for a crawler. Every page carries a canonical pointing at the
# custom domain, which is enough for Google to consolidate, but the duplicate
# still gets crawled and can still be linked. This makes the subdomain a
# permanent redirect instead.
#
# The rule matches that exact host, so Netlify's deploy previews and branch
# deploys — deploy-preview-N--<site>.netlify.app — are untouched and stay
# browsable. `301!` forces the redirect: without the bang, a request for a
# path that exists as a static file (which is all of them) would be served
# rather than redirected.

https://vaavkitchenandcaterers.netlify.app/*  https://vaavkitchenandcaterers.com/:splat  301!

# Every page is also reachable at its explicit index.html — /services/ and
# /services/index.html both returned 200, so each page had a second URL. Both
# carry the same canonical, pointing at the clean form, and none of the
# index.html URLs are indexed, so this was never the active problem; it is
# closed here because a duplicate surface that costs nothing to remove should
# not be left open.
#
# Listed one per page rather than pattern-matched: a Netlify splat only binds
# at the end of a path, so no single rule covers both /about/index.html and
# /menu/tiffin/index.html. Nine pages is few enough to be explicit, and the
# list is checked by the redirect test below.
#
# These need the forcing bang for the same reason as the rule above: each
# index.html is a real file in the publish directory and would otherwise be
# served rather than redirected. Requests for the clean URL are unaffected —
# a rule matches the requested path, and "/" is not "/index.html".

/index.html               /               301!
/about/index.html         /about/         301!
/contact/index.html       /contact/       301!
/corporate/index.html     /corporate/     301!
/services/index.html      /services/      301!
/menu/index.html          /menu/          301!
/menu/tiffin/index.html   /menu/tiffin/   301!
/menu/lunch/index.html    /menu/lunch/    301!
/menu/dinner/index.html   /menu/dinner/   301!

# site/ is both the Netlify publish directory and the npm project root, so the
# files that say how the site is built and tested are served alongside the site
# itself. /package.json, /server.cjs and the five test files all answer 200 in
# production. None of it is secret and none of it is interesting on its own,
# but none of it is site content either: the dependency list is the part a
# stranger can actually use, matched against published advisories, and the
# surface grows every time a tool drops a config file beside the source.
# ADR-0005 moved the documents out and left this half open; ADR-0007 left it
# open again, because `_headers` can add a header to a response but has no way
# to refuse to send one.
#
# A redirect does. Each of these serves the 404 page under a 404 status, so the
# path answers exactly as a path that was never there does.
#
# The bang matters more here than anywhere else in this file. Every one of
# these paths is a real file sitting in the publish directory — precisely the
# case where an unforced rule loses to the file and the file is served anyway.
# Unforced, these rules would read correctly and do nothing at all.
#
# Listed one per file for the same reason the index.html rules are: a Netlify
# splat binds only at the end of a path, so there is no /*.test.js. The test
# below fails if a published file that is not site content has no rule here,
# and fails just as loudly if a rule ever appears for a file the pages load.

/README.md              /404.html   404!
/package.json           /404.html   404!
/package-lock.json      /404.html   404!
/vitest.config.js       /404.html   404!
/server.cjs             /404.html   404!
/.gitignore             /404.html   404!
/.claude/launch.json    /404.html   404!
/chrome-sync.test.js    /404.html   404!
/menu-data.test.js      /404.html   404!
/menu-pages.test.js     /404.html   404!
/redirects.test.js      /404.html   404!
/responsive.test.js     /404.html   404!
/shortlist.test.js      /404.html   404!
